245
00:09:46,509 --> 00:09:48,102
Well, we can't just abandon it.

246
00:09:48,217 --> 00:09:50,312
It's almost dark.
That's prime Glossner time.

247
00:09:50,455 --> 00:09:52,803
Our kids are living
in an old picnic table.

248
00:09:52,924 --> 00:09:54,044
Even for us, that's weird.

249
00:09:54,172 --> 00:09:56,277
Look, I've got
a plan to fix this.

250
00:09:56,414 --> 00:09:58,962
Let's say we buy her
a new hose,

251
00:09:59,073 --> 00:10:00,262
just to keep the peace.

252
00:10:00,392 --> 00:10:02,006
We can't do that.
That's admitting guilt.

253
00:10:02,131 --> 00:10:04,441
Rain of fire, Mike.
Rain of fire.

254
00:10:04,566 --> 00:10:05,985
So that's it?
This is our life now?

255
00:10:06,149 --> 00:10:07,921
Pretty much.

256
00:10:08,072 --> 00:10:10,721
Unless I end up being
a really successful...

257
00:10:11,198 --> 00:10:13,782
car salesman. Seriously?

258
00:10:24,271 --> 00:10:26,189
You know, I should
probably stay here

259
00:10:26,298 --> 00:10:27,910
and keep guard tomorrow, too.

260
00:10:28,134 --> 00:10:30,083
Guess I'll never know
what's going on down there.

261
00:10:30,193 --> 00:10:32,665
Dude, you're gonna want
to know that stuff.

262
00:10:33,035 --> 00:10:36,034
Trust me, one day, you're gonna
be just as excited about girls

263
00:10:36,149 --> 00:10:37,610
as you are about books.

264
00:10:38,180 --> 00:10:39,978
I don't really
see that happening.

265
00:10:40,260 --> 00:10:42,959
Okay. When you go a day
without reading a book,

266
00:10:43,110 --> 00:10:45,010
how do you feel?

267
00:10:45,766 --> 00:10:47,235
Like I'm going crazy.

268
00:10:47,342 --> 00:10:48,936
I just wanna get
my hands on one.

269
00:10:49,059 --> 00:10:50,457
Exactly.
That's how you're gonna feel

270
00:10:50,564 --> 00:10:51,726
about girls some day.

271
00:10:52,544 --> 00:10:53,450
I don't know.

272
00:10:54,064 --> 00:10:56,429
I'm still confused about
all that stuff in the movie.

273
00:10:56,696 --> 00:10:59,025
Maybe I should just go
to the library and research it.

274
00:10:59,144 --> 00:11:01,918
You don't need the library.
That's what the ax-man's for.

275
00:11:02,307 --> 00:11:03,022
Huh?

276
00:11:03,437 --> 00:11:04,476
Let me break this down
for you...

277
00:11:05,485 --> 00:11:08,313
<i>So over the next two hours,</i>
<i>Axl explained everything...</i>

278
00:11:08,873 --> 00:11:10,833
<i>in graphic detail.</i>

279
00:11:18,248 --> 00:11:19,629
And that's...

280
00:11:19,762 --> 00:11:21,012
why you gotta pretend to listen

281
00:11:21,119 --> 00:11:22,902
when chicks talk
about their feelings.

282
00:11:26,553 --> 00:11:28,952
<i>I know, I know.</i>
<i>Not my best moment.</i>

283
00:11:29,100 --> 00:11:30,963
<i>Mike's usually</i>
<i>pretty smart about things.</i>

284
00:11:31,174 --> 00:11:32,139
<i>But if you ask me,</i>

285
00:11:32,238 --> 00:11:35,660
<i>$13.99 is a small price</i>
<i>to pay for peace.</i>

286
00:11:35,885 --> 00:11:37,705
<i>Like the Peyton Manning</i>
<i>football I gave him</i>

287
00:11:37,803 --> 00:11:39,627
<i>that wasn't really signed</i>
<i>by Peyton Manning,</i>

288
00:11:39,775 --> 00:11:42,104
<i>he just doesn't need to know.</i>

289
00:11:45,304 --> 00:11:46,772
<i>Wow. For someone</i>
<i>with such big feet,</i>

290
00:11:46,891 --> 00:11:48,027
<i>she sure is quiet.</i>

291
00:11:48,130 --> 00:11:50,234
What are <i>you</i> doing in <i>my</i> yard?

292
00:11:50,587 --> 00:11:54,101
Oh, I, uh, was,
uh, walking at night,

293
00:11:54,237 --> 00:11:56,699
you know, like I always do.
You've probably seen me.

294
00:11:56,848 --> 00:11:58,058
And I noticed that, uh,

295
00:11:58,203 --> 00:12:00,154
oh, your hose is here
after all.

296
00:12:00,264 --> 00:12:01,729
Isn't that funny?

297
00:12:01,839 --> 00:12:03,016
That's not my hose.

298
00:12:03,198 --> 00:12:05,478
Oh, I don't know.
I'm pretty sure it is.

299
00:12:05,599 --> 00:12:08,524
It looks like it.
Squirts water.

300
00:12:08,823 --> 00:12:10,077
Mine's orange.

301
00:12:11,090 --> 00:12:12,917
Really? Huh.

302
00:12:13,181 --> 00:12:15,689
Who would have guessed?
That's such a rare color.

303
00:12:16,298 --> 00:12:17,981
Well, a hose is a hose.

304
00:12:18,166 --> 00:12:19,828
Here, go ahead.
Take it.

305
00:12:19,963 --> 00:12:21,339
I don't want that crappy hose.

306
00:12:21,845 --> 00:12:23,405
Well, yeah,
this is even better.

307
00:12:23,517 --> 00:12:25,339
I mean, your hose was old
and beaten up,

308
00:12:25,465 --> 00:12:27,421
and look-- this is all shiny
and brand-new.

309
00:12:27,546 --> 00:12:29,453
You sure do know
a lot about my hose

310
00:12:29,577 --> 00:12:31,044
for someone who didn't take it.

311
00:12:31,157 --> 00:12:32,162
Hose thief!

312
00:12:33,105 --> 00:12:35,786
Okay, that's it.
I am a good neighbor.

313
00:12:35,978 --> 00:12:38,182
I don't steal.
My family doesn't steal.

314
00:12:38,312 --> 00:12:40,233
<i>Your</i> family's
the one who steals!

315
00:12:40,328 --> 00:12:41,297
I don't like
what you're implying.

316
00:12:41,392 --> 00:12:42,165
I'm not implying anything.

317
00:12:42,264 --> 00:12:44,385
It's a fact. Your kids
are a bunch of hooligans!

318
00:12:44,494 --> 00:12:45,758
They take everything
in the neighborhood--

319
00:12:45,887 --> 00:12:47,964
bikes, toys, shrubbery.

320
00:12:48,074 --> 00:12:50,855
Don't you talk about my kids.
Them's good boys.

321
00:12:50,975 --> 00:12:54,475
- Where you been at?!
- None of your damn business.

322
00:12:58,834 --> 00:13:00,158
You expect me to believe

323
00:13:00,288 --> 00:13:02,233
that you're dumb enough
to bring back a hose

324
00:13:02,355 --> 00:13:04,359
that you didn't even take
in the first place?

325
00:13:04,572 --> 00:13:05,529
Fine. You know what?

326
00:13:05,656 --> 00:13:07,524
I tried to be nice,
but I'm done.

327
00:13:07,731 --> 00:13:10,537
I'm taking it home.
It's my hose now.

328
00:13:10,627 --> 00:13:12,591
Oh, so you're gonna steal it
a second time?

329
00:13:12,703 --> 00:13:15,433
You said you didn't want it!
It's on my property!

330
00:13:15,987 --> 00:13:18,019
No! I'm taking it back!
Let go!

331
00:13:18,145 --> 00:13:19,465
You let go!

332
00:13:19,575 --> 00:13:22,627
It's not your hose, lady!
You said you didn't want it! Give it!

333
00:13:22,763 --> 00:13:24,431
Uhh!

334
00:13:25,223 --> 00:13:26,378
Ow.

335
00:13:36,594 --> 00:13:37,278
Morning.

336
00:13:38,240 --> 00:13:39,019
Morning.

337
00:13:39,124 --> 00:13:40,075
Is there coffee?

338
00:13:40,190 --> 00:13:41,339
<i>Yep.</i>

339
00:13:44,822 --> 00:13:45,795
Somethin' wrong?

340
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:48,179
Okay, if I tell you,

341
00:13:48,278 --> 00:13:49,764
you have to promise
not to get mad.

342
00:13:50,306 --> 00:13:51,505
I can't make that promise.

343
00:13:52,456 --> 00:13:54,303
Something happened last night.

344
00:13:56,436 --> 00:13:58,006
What the hell?

345
00:13:58,625 --> 00:14:00,810
- How'd you do that?
- I went over to the Glossners'.

346
00:14:01,014 --> 00:14:04,203
Frankie, I told you
that was a bad idea.

347
00:14:04,369 --> 00:14:05,440
She didn't hit you, did she?

348
00:14:05,555 --> 00:14:06,824
No, the hose did.

349
00:14:06,989 --> 00:14:08,559
What, she found the hose?

350
00:14:08,751 --> 00:14:10,555
Not exactly.

351
00:14:11,405 --> 00:14:12,812
Look, I know you
didn't love the idea,

352
00:14:12,924 --> 00:14:14,961
but I bought her a new hose
and went over there to leave it.

353
00:14:15,082 --> 00:14:16,423
But Rita caught me,
and she called me a thief,

354
00:14:16,560 --> 00:14:17,483
which, I mean, come on.

355
00:14:17,578 --> 00:14:19,398
So we got in a fight,
and the hose chipped my tooth.

356
00:14:19,502 --> 00:14:21,420
Listen, I don't want to hear
a bunch of "I told you sos."

357
00:14:21,520 --> 00:14:23,058
How many do I get?
Give me a number.

358
00:14:23,173 --> 00:14:24,405
Look, I did the honorable thing

359
00:14:24,508 --> 00:14:26,000
and snuck over there
in the middle of the night.

360
00:14:26,105 --> 00:14:28,058
Could you cover your mouth
while you talk?

361
00:14:28,268 --> 00:14:29,442
It's that noticeable?

362
00:14:29,620 --> 00:14:30,892
You're actually
starting to look like

363
00:14:31,032 --> 00:14:32,342
you're in our income bracket.

364
00:14:32,807 --> 00:14:33,920
It's that bad, huh?

365
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:36,681
Ah, I'd better call the dentist
and see if he can squeeze me in

366
00:14:36,827 --> 00:14:39,156
before Ehlert realizes
I'm still on his insurance.

367
00:14:45,462 --> 00:14:47,570
Mr. Heck, how <i>are</i> you?

368
00:14:48,158 --> 00:14:50,819
Fine.
Sue, your friends are here!

369
00:14:50,950 --> 00:14:52,278
Be out in a minute!

370
00:14:53,927 --> 00:14:55,322
Brad and I are taking Sue
to the mall,

371
00:14:55,513 --> 00:14:58,084
but don't worry, we're not
gonna spend any money.

372
00:14:58,216 --> 00:14:59,845
Because <i>things</i>
don't make you happy.

373
00:14:59,958 --> 00:15:00,786
People do.

374
00:15:00,920 --> 00:15:02,599
But if Sue wants a Fro-Yo,
I can pay for it

375
00:15:02,718 --> 00:15:05,108
with the money I made juggling
at the ren fair this summer.

376
00:15:05,225 --> 00:15:06,654
That's short
for "renaissance."

377
00:15:06,936 --> 00:15:08,330
You don't have to
explain everything.

378
00:15:08,505 --> 00:15:10,886
Oh! I almost forgot.
I come bearing gifts.

379
00:15:11,742 --> 00:15:14,668
For Brick, some of
my favorite hand-me downs.

380
00:15:15,010 --> 00:15:18,319
For Mrs. Heck,
the Ali MacGraw yoga workout.

381
00:15:18,443 --> 00:15:20,485
It's like an antidepressant
in a VHS tape.

382
00:15:20,677 --> 00:15:23,391
And for you, Mr. Heck,
a hug.

383
00:15:24,005 --> 00:15:25,887
Hey, Sue! You don't want
to keep your friends waiting!

384
00:15:29,423 --> 00:15:31,597
Anyway, uh,
it's nice of you guys

385
00:15:31,680 --> 00:15:32,802
to get Sue out of the house.

386
00:15:32,928 --> 00:15:34,566
She's been kind of down
since they told her

387
00:15:34,671 --> 00:15:36,271
that the mascots
can't go on that trip.

388
00:15:36,551 --> 00:15:38,362
What? Yeah, they can.

389
00:15:38,923 --> 00:15:41,777
No, I think
you're wrong, Carly.

390
00:15:44,152 --> 00:15:46,665
You know what?
Uh, you guys go on ahead.

391
00:15:46,838 --> 00:15:48,209
I gotta talk
to Sue about something.

392
00:15:48,323 --> 00:15:49,535
Okay, but remember,
Mr. Heck,

393
00:15:49,657 --> 00:15:50,594
I'm not just her friend.

394
00:15:50,702 --> 00:15:52,649
I'm here for you, too, 24/7.

395
00:15:52,796 --> 00:15:55,670
Tweet me. We can also
Facebook, Skype, G-Chat.

396
00:15:55,787 --> 00:15:57,711
- You want me to write this all down?
- I'm good.

397
00:15:57,881 --> 00:15:58,956
Okay.

398
00:16:01,657 --> 00:16:03,634
Hey. So I was just wondering,

399
00:16:03,742 --> 00:16:06,032
who exactly decided
you couldn't go on this trip?

400
00:16:08,064 --> 00:16:09,808
I saw your paycheck, okay?

401
00:16:09,928 --> 00:16:11,640
I am so, so sorry.

402
00:16:11,753 --> 00:16:13,094
It was just sitting there
on the desk,

403
00:16:13,211 --> 00:16:15,039
a-and they didn't lick
the sticky part,

404
00:16:15,154 --> 00:16:17,199
so it was open, and I looked,
and I saw how much you make,

405
00:16:17,311 --> 00:16:19,060
and my trip costs
too much money.

406
00:16:19,194 --> 00:16:20,273
I don't wanna go!

407
00:16:20,393 --> 00:16:21,901
What? Sue, what are you
talking about?

408
00:16:22,862 --> 00:16:24,233
I know you don't
get paid a lot of money.

409
00:16:24,430 --> 00:16:26,398
A-and I am a horrible person

410
00:16:26,518 --> 00:16:28,063
because I am always
asking for stuff,

411
00:16:28,206 --> 00:16:31,042
and mom doesn't have a job,
and you work all the time,

412
00:16:31,215 --> 00:16:33,779
and our TV has a weird,
squiggly line down the middle.

413
00:16:33,938 --> 00:16:35,645
But just last week,
I had mom buy me

414
00:16:35,770 --> 00:16:37,271
a "girls rule the world"
pencil case.

415
00:16:37,408 --> 00:16:38,949
I am so selfish!

416
00:16:39,125 --> 00:16:41,408
Sue, you're not selfish.
You're a normal kid.

417
00:16:41,662 --> 00:16:44,136
But I already know
girls rule the world.

418
00:16:44,261 --> 00:16:46,281
So do I really need to read it
on a pencil case?

419
00:16:46,427 --> 00:16:48,458
It's like I am just
throwing money away!

420
00:16:48,572 --> 00:16:49,712
Hey, hey, stop.

421
00:16:49,809 --> 00:16:50,825
Okay, listen, you're right.

422
00:16:51,768 --> 00:16:52,430
I am?

423
00:16:52,542 --> 00:16:56,036
Yeah. We don't have a lot
of extra money right now.

424
00:16:56,172 --> 00:16:58,080
Oh. Okay.

425
00:16:58,248 --> 00:16:59,936
But it's not your job
to worry about it.

426
00:17:00,254 --> 00:17:01,924
I'm the dad. It's my job.

427
00:17:02,133 --> 00:17:03,898
And I say "no"
to plenty of stuff.

428
00:17:04,133 --> 00:17:06,693
And this trip is a big deal.
You worked hard.

429
00:17:06,819 --> 00:17:08,443
So... we can do it.

430
00:17:08,556 --> 00:17:09,946
But your paycheck.

431
00:17:10,084 --> 00:17:11,841
If that's what you make
every two weeks,

432
00:17:11,971 --> 00:17:13,788
my trip is too expensive.

433
00:17:13,928 --> 00:17:15,510
Sue, you didn't look
close enough.

434
00:17:15,611 --> 00:17:16,898
I get paid every week.

435
00:17:17,005 --> 00:17:17,986
You do?

436
00:17:18,105 --> 00:17:18,972
Yeah.

437
00:17:19,082 --> 00:17:21,485
Now go get your costume.
The band needs its chicken.

438
00:17:22,290 --> 00:17:23,481
Are you sure?

439
00:17:23,800 --> 00:17:25,932
Go, honey.
Have a good time.

440
00:17:26,150 --> 00:17:28,989
I'm going to a band competition
in Cincinnati!

441
00:17:29,092 --> 00:17:31,234
How could I not?! Aah!

442
00:17:37,722 --> 00:17:39,399
You get paid every two weeks.

443
00:17:39,519 --> 00:17:40,535
Yeah.

444
00:17:40,774 --> 00:17:43,983
But just like that autographed
Justin Bieber hat we got her,

445
00:17:44,147 --> 00:17:45,274
she doesn't need to know.

446
00:17:46,355 --> 00:17:49,054
It's a mighty
fine thing you done.

447
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:50,409
Go get that fixed.

448
00:17:50,734 --> 00:17:51,541
On my way.

449
00:18:17,171 --> 00:18:18,581
Are you kidding me?

450
00:18:18,709 --> 00:18:19,825
Brick, where did you get this?

451
00:18:19,927 --> 00:18:21,615
Oh, I took it
from the Glossners.

452
00:18:21,728 --> 00:18:23,827
<i>What?</i> And the whole time
I've been talking

453
00:18:23,938 --> 00:18:25,428
about the hose
that Rita thinks I stole,

454
00:18:25,551 --> 00:18:26,953
you didn't say anything?

455
00:18:28,405 --> 00:18:31,327
<i>Oh,</i> I thought you were
talking about panty hose.

456
00:18:48,817 --> 00:18:50,080
Okay, look, we just have to
get rid of this

457
00:18:50,182 --> 00:18:51,542
before anybody finds out.

458
00:18:52,514 --> 00:18:53,900
Are you sure
it's even the Glossners'?

459
00:18:54,006 --> 00:18:55,776
I think they might have
stolen it from the Donahues.

460
00:18:55,884 --> 00:18:57,745
Yeah, well the Donahues
aren't gonna punch my boobs in,

461
00:18:57,858 --> 00:18:59,431
so we're getting
rid of it anyway.

462
00:18:59,642 --> 00:19:02,730
And, Brick, we
never speak of this again.

463
00:19:02,832 --> 00:19:05,553
Just like that autographed
X Games posters we got Axl.

464
00:19:07,669 --> 00:19:10,179
Seriously, how does she
keep doing that?

465
00:19:22,151 --> 00:19:24,164
Where are you both
sneakin' off to?

466
00:19:24,823 --> 00:19:28,129
Just going to the dentist to get
my tooth fixed.

467
00:19:28,295 --> 00:19:30,648
I did that once
on a cop's belt.

468
00:19:32,163 --> 00:19:33,698
That's really funny.

469
00:19:36,884 --> 00:19:38,465
Well, we should go.

470
00:19:38,701 --> 00:19:40,893
Nobody to watch him,
so he's gotta come with me.

471
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:42,498
Not that our house
is empty right now.

472
00:19:42,657 --> 00:19:44,099
I know where my hose is.

473
00:19:45,109 --> 00:19:46,639
We don't.

474
00:19:46,883 --> 00:19:47,451
Whoop.

475
00:19:47,705 --> 00:19:48,772
Whoop.

476
00:19:49,661 --> 00:19:50,754
I'm lying.

477
00:19:51,526 --> 00:19:53,769
Somebody put it
back on my lawn.

478
00:19:54,535 --> 00:19:55,941
The orange one?

479
00:19:56,312 --> 00:19:58,754
Oh. Well... huh.

480
00:19:59,290 --> 00:20:01,519
Wow. That's great
that you got it back.

481
00:20:01,642 --> 00:20:03,281
When us Glossners
make a mistake,

482
00:20:03,367 --> 00:20:04,563
we admit it.

483
00:20:04,677 --> 00:20:06,346
That's why so many of us
is in jail.

484
00:20:06,485 --> 00:20:07,928
We've got integrity.

485
00:20:08,056 --> 00:20:12,317
Oh, yeah. That's-- that is
honorable. I appreciate it.

486
00:20:12,438 --> 00:20:14,960
So I want you all to come over
Sunday for a pool party.

487
00:20:15,266 --> 00:20:16,372
That's not necessary.

488
00:20:16,614 --> 00:20:18,782
I don't want to owe you nothing.
You're coming.

489
00:20:19,491 --> 00:20:22,584
Okay. Great.
See you then.

490
00:20:23,392 --> 00:20:25,793
<i>I never did find out how that hose
got to Rita.</i>

491
00:20:25,897 --> 00:20:27,686
<i>Probably some other</i>
<i>scared neighbor.</i>

492
00:20:27,874 --> 00:20:29,324
<i>But it's the Glossners,</i>

493
00:20:29,455 --> 00:20:31,526
<i>so Brick and I</i>
<i>made ours disappear,</i>

494
00:20:31,709 --> 00:20:32,764
<i>just in case.</i>

495
00:20:34,693 --> 00:20:37,034
<i>Brick and I never talked</i>
<i>about that night again.</i>

496
00:20:37,214 --> 00:20:39,818
<i>But he did have a lot to say</i>
<i>on another subject.</i>

497
00:20:39,938 --> 00:20:41,674
Does anyone have any questions?

498
00:20:41,801 --> 00:20:43,681
When chicks "want it,"

499
00:20:43,844 --> 00:20:47,204
do they want it right away,
or can I finish my book first?

500
00:20:47,311 --> 00:20:50,048
<i>He told the kids</i>
<i>everything Axl had told him.</i>

501
00:20:51,700 --> 00:20:53,778
<i>And the nurse told</i> us...

502
00:20:54,728 --> 00:20:56,038
<i>and we told Axl.</i>

503
00:20:56,157 --> 00:20:57,987
<i>At least he had the right info,</i>
<i>'cause it turned out,</i>

504
00:20:58,090 --> 00:20:59,856
<i>we hadn't talked</i>
<i>to any of the kids.</i>

505
00:21:00,039 --> 00:21:02,194
<i>Yep. You start going off</i>
<i>on a walk,</i>

506
00:21:02,293 --> 00:21:04,164
<i>and you never know</i>
<i>where it'll lead.</i>

507
00:21:04,262 --> 00:21:05,871
<i>If I hadn't gone</i>
<i>for a walk that day,</i>

508
00:21:05,985 --> 00:21:07,266
<i>I wouldn't have</i>
<i>chipped my tooth,</i>

509
00:21:07,398 --> 00:21:08,849
<i>which sent me</i>
<i>to the dentist's office,</i>

510
00:21:09,013 --> 00:21:09,952
<i>where I learned the girl</i>

511
00:21:10,053 --> 00:21:11,396
<i>that put the squirty thing</i>
<i>in my mouth</i>

512
00:21:11,508 --> 00:21:14,768
<i>is well paid and gets to wear</i>
<i>comfy shoes all day...</i>

513
00:21:14,872 --> 00:21:17,376
<i>which led me to finally settle</i>
<i>on my new career--</i>

514
00:21:17,526 --> 00:21:18,710
<i>dental assistant.</i>

515
00:21:18,825 --> 00:21:20,945
<i>'Cause believe me, if there's</i>
<i>one thing I've learned,</i>

516
00:21:21,073 --> 00:21:22,817
<i>teeth are important.</i>

517
00:21:23,207 --> 00:21:25,375
- Another beer?
- Sure.

518
00:21:25,480 --> 00:21:27,204
Then run over to your house
and get us some.

519
00:21:27,573 --> 00:21:29,040
I'll keep an eye on your kids.

520
